     "<br>\n<br>\n<br>\n<blockquote style=\"padding-left:5px;margin-left:5px;border-left:#b6b6b6 2px solid;margin-right:0\">\n\t-----Original Messages-----<br>\n<b>From:</b><span>&quot;章仲恒&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">zh_zha...@zju.edu.cn</a>&gt;</span><br>\n<b>Sent Time:</b><span>2018-04-23 06:38:22 (Monday)</span><br>\n<b>To:</b> &quot;joshua rosenberg&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">jro...@msu.edu</a>&gt;<br>\n<b>Cc:</b> <br>\n<b>Subject:</b> Re: Re: Re: Re: latent profile analysis<br>\n<br>\nDear <span style=\"white-space:normal\">Rosenberg</span><br>\n\t<p>\n\t\tSorry for disturbing you again. \n\t</p>\n\t<p>\n\t\tIn the latest version, I cannot find which function to perform the <span style=\"white-space:normal\">VLMR. </span> \n\t</p>\n\t<p>\n\t\t<span style=\"white-space:normal\">Can you post an example in the page <a href=\"https://jrosen48.github.io/tidyLPA/\" style=\"white-space:normal\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://jrosen48.github.io/tidyLPA/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792496192000000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1nYEdNg6nixS3LwV9M5Mvy\">https://jrosen48.github.io/tidyLPA/</a>     </span> \n\t</p>\n<br>\n\t<blockquote name=\"replyContent\" style=\"padding-left:5px;margin-left:5px;border-left:#b6b6b6 2px solid;margin-right:0\">\n\t\t-----Original Messages-----<br>\n<b>From:</b><span>&quot;章仲恒&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">zh_zha...@zju.edu.cn</a>&gt;</span><br>\n<b>Sent Time:</b><span>2018-04-02 06:15:05 (Monday)</span><br>\n<b>To:</b> &quot;joshua rosenberg&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">jro...@msu.edu</a>&gt;<br>\n<b>Cc:</b> <br>\n<b>Subject:</b> Re: Re: Re: latent profile analysis<br>\n<br>\nThat&#39;s great, I really appreciated your help!<br>\n<br>\n<br>\n\t\t<blockquote name=\"replyContent\" style=\"padding-left:5px;margin-left:5px;border-left:#b6b6b6 2px solid;margin-right:0\">\n\t\t\t-----Original Messages-----<br>\n<b>From:</b><span>&quot;Joshua Rosenberg&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">jro...@msu.edu</a>&gt;</span><br>\n<b>Sent Time:</b><span>2018-04-02 01:32:56 (Monday)</span><br>\n<b>To:</b> &quot;章仲恒&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">zh_zha...@zju.edu.cn</a>&gt;<br>\n<b>Cc:</b> <br>\n<b>Subject:</b> Re: Re: latent profile analysis<br>\n<br>\n\t\t\t<div dir=\"ltr\">\n\t\t\t\tHi there, I have added VLMR to the latest version: <a href=\"https://jrosen48.github.io/tidyLPA/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://jrosen48.github.io/tidyLPA/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792496192000000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1nYEdNg6nixS3LwV9M5Mvy\">https://jrosen48.github.io/tidyLPA/</a> \n\t\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<br>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t\tThank you your question.\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t\tJosh<br>\n<br>\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"gmail_quote\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div dir=\"ltr\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tOn Sun, Feb 11, 2018 at 5:27 PM 章仲恒 &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">zh_zha...@zju.edu.cn</a>&gt; wrote:<br>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tMany thanks for your reply. I am going to install Mplus, and would like to perform <span style=\"white-space:normal\">VLMR LRT and adjusted VLMR LRT</span>. Can you also make changes to the tidyLPA and help me to realize these functionality?  <br>\n<br>\n<br>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<blockquote name=\"replyContent\" style=\"padding-left:5px;margin-left:5px;border-left:#b6b6b6 2px solid;margin-right:0\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t-----Original Messages-----<br>\n<b>From:</b><span>&quot;Joshua Rosenberg&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">jro...@msu.edu</a>&gt;</span><br>\n<b>Sent Time:</b><span>2018-02-11 23:12:54 (Sunday)</span><br>\n<b>To:</b> &quot;章仲恒&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">zh_zha...@zju.edu.cn</a>&gt;<br>\n<b>Cc:</b> &quot;Schmidt, Jennifer&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">jasc...@msu.edu</a>&gt;, &quot;Patrick Beymer&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">beym...@msu.edu</a>&gt;, &quot;Rebecca Steingut&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">rebeccaro...@gmail.com</a>&gt;<br>\n<b>Subject:</b> Re: latent profile analysis\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</blockquote>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<blockquote name=\"replyContent\" style=\"padding-left:5px;margin-left:5px;border-left:#b6b6b6 2px solid;margin-right:0\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<br>\n<br>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div dir=\"ltr\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tHi, thank you for your message. It is wonderful to see scholars in other countries are discovering the open-source tool that we are developing to carry out latent profile analysis. At this present time, you can only carry out the parametric bootstrapped BLRT with the boostrap_lrt() function. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<br>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tSee this page here (it is used in a way very similar to compare_solutions() and to estimate_solutions(): <a href=\"https://jrosen48.github.io/tidyLPA/reference/bootstrap_lrt.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://jrosen48.github.io/tidyLPA/reference/bootstrap_lrt.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792496192000000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3Zh5kg4iHZRGhbKFllHaJ3\">https://jrosen48.github.io/tidyLPA/reference/bootstrap_lrt.html</a> \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<br>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tIf you have any trouble using it or if you have any questions, please let us know.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<br>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tAt least based on my initial understanding, the BLRT is recommended over the VLMRT LRT and the adjusted VLMR LRT. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<br>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tRegarding the VLMR LRT and adjusted VLMR LRT, these are presently not available. The reason is that tidyLPA is an interface to the mclust software. We have implemented some statistics (SABIC, CAIC, and others) that are not available in mclust; however, based on some initial research, we&#39;ve had some trouble translating from <a href=\"https://academic.oup.com/biomet/article-abstract/88/3/767/340113\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://academic.oup.com/biomet/article-abstract/88/3/767/340113&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792496192000000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3XyxXOyGcJTOyr7200q67X\">the publication introducing VLMR LRT by Vuong, Lo, Mendell, and Rubin</a>. Accordingly, the way that we have been able to carry out these tests is using the MPlus software. If you have MPlus, we have written a number of functions that allow you to use it through R/tidyLPA (i.e., <a href=\"https://jrosen48.github.io/tidyLPA/reference/compare_solutions_mplus.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://jrosen48.github.io/tidyLPA/reference/compare_solutions_mplus.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792496192000000&amp;usg=AOvVaw393FOtleGuvkhQ0yZbwR5-\">estimate_solutions_mplus()</a> and others, see <a href=\"https://jrosen48.github.io/tidyLPA/reference/index.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://jrosen48.github.io/tidyLPA/reference/index.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792496192000000&amp;usg=AOvVaw225fF4qRsLX4ufNfB3-aAW\">here</a>). However, we have not added functionality to carry out VLMRT LRT and adjusted VLMRT LRT through R/tidyLPA quite yet. If you do have MPlus, we could make these changes quickly. If not and you need to wait for them to be implemented in the other functions - those that do not use MPlus - then that may take awhile (again, because they are not implemented in the mclust package that tidyLPA is an interface to).\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<br>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tThank you again for your message - I hope that this helps you to at least be able to carry out the BLRT. The VLMR LRT tests may take a while longer - I hope you understand. Be in touch with any questions and, if you would, to let us know for what purpose you are using the package.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<br>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tSincerely,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tJoshua Rosenberg\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n<br>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"gmail_quote\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div dir=\"ltr\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tOn Sun, Feb 11, 2018 at 6:31 AM 章仲恒 &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">zh_zha...@zju.edu.cn</a>&gt; wrote:<br>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tDear Pro. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</p>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tI am interested in your post on <a href=\"https://jrosen48.github.io/blog/lpa-in-r-using-mclust/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://jrosen48.github.io/blog/lpa-in-r-using-mclust/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792496192000000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1vFnO2EF-vt69nZm5YUB0n\">https://jrosen48.github.io/blog/lpa-in-r-using-mclust/</a> \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</p>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tHowever, I also want to calculate Vuong-Lo-Mendell-Rubin likelihood ratio test\n(LRT), Lo-Mendell-Rubin adjusted likelihood ratio test (adjusted LRT),\nparametric bootstrapped likelihood ratio test (BLRT). How may I do that? \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</p>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<br>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</p>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<br>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</p>\n<br>\n<br>\n<br>\n<span> \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<hr align=\"left\" style=\"margin:0.5em 0;width:30em;min-height:1px;background-color:#999;border:none\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<span style=\"font-size:18.6667px;white-space:normal;font-family:&#39;Comic Sans MS&#39;\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria,serif;font-size:12pt\">Dr. Zhongheng Zhang</span></span><span></span> \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<span style=\"font-family:Cambria,serif;font-size:12pt\">Department of emergency medicine, Sir Run-Run Shaw Hospital, Zhejiang University School of Medicine, Hangzhou, 310016, China. </span><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Comic Sans MS&#39;\"><br>\n</span> \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n<span style=\"white-space:normal;font-family:Cambria,serif;font-size:12pt\"></span><span></span> \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<span style=\"font-family:&#39;Comic Sans MS&#39;\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria,serif;font-size:12pt\">Members of the Zhejiang society of evidence based medicine and epidemiology</span></span> \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n<span style=\"white-space:normal;font-family:Cambria,serif;font-size:12pt\"></span><span></span> \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<span style=\"font-family:&#39;Comic Sans MS&#39;\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria,serif;font-size:12pt\">Section editor of Journal of thoracic disease</span></span> \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<span style=\"font-family:&#39;Comic Sans MS&#39;;font-size:x-small\"></span> \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n<span style=\"font-family:Cambria,serif;font-size:12pt\"></span> \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Zhongheng_Zhang\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Zhongheng_Zhang&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792496192000000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0QhWD_kbPnJpSZ79lyBXW8\"><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Comic Sans MS&#39;;color:#000000;font-size:x-small\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria,serif;font-size:12pt\">https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Zhongheng_Zhang</span></span></a> \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n<span style=\"font-family:Cambria,serif;font-size:12pt\"></span> \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://publons.com/author/239344/zhongheng-zhang#profile\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://publons.com/author/239344/zhongheng-zhang%23profile&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792496192000000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2907jKzlD6vBvjLsUZ8JMp\"><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Comic Sans MS&#39;;color:#000000;font-size:x-small\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria,serif;font-size:12pt\">https://publons.com/author/239344/zhongheng-zhang#profile</span></span></a> \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n</span> \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</blockquote>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n-- <br>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div dir=\"ltr\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div dir=\"ltr\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div style=\"color:#222222;font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.7273px;line-height:normal\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div style=\"font-size:12.8px\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tJoshua Rosenberg, Ph.D. Candidate\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div style=\"font-size:12.8px\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t